    "lines": [
      {
        "snippetId": "s1382",
        "messageOrdinal": 95,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1845-09-04",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "4 September 1845",
        "text": "Indeed my headaches are not worth enquiring about--I mean, they are not of the slightest consequence, and seldom survive the remedy of a cup of coffee.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s3640",
        "messageOrdinal": 202,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-01-17",
        "approximate": true,
        "dateLabel": "c. 17 January 1846",
        "text": "It may be wrong and ungrateful, but I do wish sometimes that the world were away--even the good Kenyon-aspect of the world.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s4668",
        "messageOrdinal": 248,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-02-27",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "27 February 1846",
        "text": "There is room too on it for the feet of a bird!",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s4745",
        "messageOrdinal": 250,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-03-02",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "2 March 1846",
        "text": "And this I felt in my guess, long before I knew you.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s4784",
        "messageOrdinal": 253,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-03-03",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "3 March 1846",
        "text": "Then dear Mr. Kenyon talked of the poems; and hoped, very earnestly I am sure, that you would finish 'Saul'--which you ought to do, must do--only not now.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s5025",
        "messageOrdinal": 263,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-03-11",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "11 March 1846",
        "text": "You know from my letter how I found you out in the matter of the 'Soul's Tragedy.'",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s5191",
        "messageOrdinal": 272,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-03-18",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "18 March 1846",
        "text": "Ah well--we shall see.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s5942",
        "messageOrdinal": 305,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-04-09",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "9 April 1846",
        "text": "After the question about the ‘Sirens’ song to Ulysses, dearest?",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s8924",
        "messageOrdinal": 434,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-07-03",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "3 July 1846",
        "text": "And if you love me only nearly as much (instead of the prodigal ‘more’) afterward, I shall be satisfied, and shall not run from you further than to the bottom of the page.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s9989",
        "messageOrdinal": 478,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-07-30",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "30 July 1846",
        "text": "I have come back to live a little for you—.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s12056",
        "messageOrdinal": 554,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-09-11",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "11 September 1846",
        "text": "And then, you shall have the ring ... soon enough and safer.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      }
    ]
  }
}
